MNF15-P1-D D1 gate log (2026-11-14) — exact probe-result memoization

D1 mechanism (two exact layers, same contract):
  D1a body memo : (probe configuration, FULL body bytes) -> compressed
    length. Identity decided by memcmp on the full body; the FNV-1a 64
    hash only locates the bucket. Per-pick lifetime; body-byte budget 8
    MiB (48 B/entry conservative charge); exhaustion falls back to the
    ordinary (uncached) probe — correct by construction.
  D1b tile memo : the laws+flat segment (modes 6|7|8 lattice) is a PURE
    function of (tile.data, planar, probe configuration) — no predictor
    residual (it consumes tile.data, not the med/med_pred body), no tile
    position, KIND-independent (the four predictor sweeps share every
    key) — so one ~1.7 KB entry replaces ~103 stored probe bodies
    (~84 KB at body budget) per sharing sweep. Same memcmp/budget
    contract; 8 MiB tile budget.

D1 gate tests (all green, src/mnf6.rs tests::p1d_d1_gates):
  p1d_forced_collision        : a collision-shaped multi-entry bucket
    planted with a NON-matching earlier entry — the memcmp skips it and
    resolves b to its own cost; a correctly misses, stores, hits.
  p1d_same_body_different_theta: the same body under Zlib-vs-Zstd3 probe
    configurations stays two identities (2 misses, 2 hits, no aliasing).
  p1d_budget_exhaustion       : budget 600 B — exactly 2 entries stored,
    the other 5 probes run uncached, EVERY cost equals the true
    compression length, `charged` accounts 2x248 exactly.
  Release suite: 91 tests / 0 failed (65 lib incl. the 3 D1 gates);
    fmt + clippy -D warnings + rustdoc clean.

