Budget-exhaustion telemetry (the honest ceiling report):
  The D0 aggregate ceiling (9.82x compressor-call reduction) assumes the
  FULL distinct-body sets stay cached: ~55k bodies on screenshot alone
  (~36-40 MB body-mem) — a knob Jon reserved, not a law. Within the
  16 MiB budget the body memo reaches D0's screenshot mass only through
  the tile layer; the residual executing mass is atlas-derived bodies
  (~560k of 676k executions on screenshot) whose full coverage needs the
  larger budget. `exhausted` counters in the census quantify the gap; the
  budget is a constant, trivially tunable if Jon rules +RSS acceptable.

Wire: untouched. Decoder: untouched. Candidates/ranks/ties: untouched
  (the memo returns the true cost of the same mathematical input).
